Summary: Minimal, fully offline home-screen launcher
Description: MinLauncher is a personal fork of Olauncher with the same goal:
 a minimalist home screen with large typography and nothing else.

 It shows your chosen apps on the home screen; swipe up to open the app
 drawer, swipe down to expand notifications, long-press for settings.
 Home-screen apps, gestures, hidden apps and text size are configurable.

 The launcher is fully offline: it does not hold the INTERNET permission
 and contains no analytics or crash reporting.

 It requests QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES because enumerating installed apps is the
 core function of any launcher (app drawer, picking apps for the home
 screen and gestures). The list of installed apps never leaves the device.

RepoType: git
Repo: https://github.com/ouj4k2q5/Minlauncher.git

# Kept in sync with each release by scripts/tag-release.sh (newest Builds entry on
# top, CurrentVersion* moved to it). Entries reference the release commit's full
# hash, as F-Droid's build metadata reference asks (not a tag name); app/build.gradle.kts
# reads version.properties directly, so no prebuild step is needed to inject the version.
Builds:
 - versionName: 0.0.2
   versionCode: 2
   commit: 31833711a45d5830a52e9172f5c9524a06d4d007
   gradle:
     - yes

AutoUpdateMode: Version
UpdateCheckMode: Tags
# Points F-Droid's tag-based update checker at the literal version committed
# to version.properties, instead of the default AndroidManifest.xml/build.gradle.kts
# scan (which would only find a Gradle property reference, not a literal).
UpdateCheckData: version.properties|versionCode=(\d+)|version.properties|versionName=(.+)
CurrentVersion: 0.0.2
CurrentVersionCode: 2
